<node id="Carbon Credits">
  <data key="d0">Carbon Credits</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbon Credits are financial instruments that represent a reduction of one metric ton of carbon dioxide emissions, expected to be issued in relation to the carbon monitoring from the restoration project.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon credits are generated through Karaguá's carbon sequestration efforts in mangroves, intended for sale to companies with decarbonization goals.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon credits represent a permit allowing the holder to emit a certain amount of carbon dioxide or other greenhouse gases, with a focus on reducing emissions.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon credits are financial instruments representing the reduction of one metric ton of carbon dioxide emissions, which can be generated through environmental projects.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon credits are units representing a reduction, removal, or sequestration of carbon dioxide, used to help organizations achieve sustainability targets.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon credits refer to financial tools that the project may seek to incorporate for sponsorship through applicable laws.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a84de646898e4c0c15a05010e9f0872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96cfbacbd794cb84c14c05802c670b7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8391c4fcd2580effc0f006b72bb8036&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfd11d7c2c4bd3494e41a898407867fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cf377716ee26ede13962ee6334fc04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56fa52e6f66e339f041d2b2bcfa35c9f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
