<node id="Manguezais">
  <data key="d0">Manguezais</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Manguezais refers to mangroves, which play a crucial role in the environment and are a focus for restoration and monitoring efforts.&lt;SEP&gt;Manguezais are coastal ecosystems recognized for their key role in carbon sequestration and their importance for biodiversity and traditional livelihoods.&lt;SEP&gt;Manguezais refer to mangrove ecosystems in Brazil, significant for their biodiversity and role in coastal protection and carbon sequestration.&lt;SEP&gt;Manguezais, or mangroves, are coastal ecosystems that are recognized as climate assets under the environmental strategies outlined by various laws and programs in Brazil.&lt;SEP&gt;Manguezais play a crucial role in carbon storage, marine species reproduction, and protecting the coastline against erosion and extreme weather events.&lt;SEP&gt;Manguezais are coastal ecosystems crucial for the identity and resources of the community in Balneário Barra do Sul.&lt;SEP&gt;Manguezais are ecosystems of mangrove trees that play a critical role in the local culture and economy of Balneário Barra do Sul.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-97956bf3a635abdaa08720534d192565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab5216ced144c274bc01b9f76450bfe1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8391c4fcd2580effc0f006b72bb8036&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-801a0e33323bfe79b6cbfaaca8800a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daf3f3a511399d27baaafacc8a1db9af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de97259662535ffc45aa87131b91edcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b1e215cb25487527b01e8441005cff0</data>
