  <data key="d0">50% of Baía da Babitonga</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The goal of Karaguá Ecotech is to impact 50% of Baía da Babitonga by 2035, benefiting over 400 families in that region.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab5216ced144c274bc01b9f76450bfe1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779674647</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fase 2">
  <data key="d0">Fase 2</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Fase 2 refers to the stage in the project focused on selecting priority areas for planting and restoration, providing training, and remunerating participants.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dac9ac0e037b36bcaa7b84fc97e0480a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779674647</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joinville">
  <data key="d0">Joinville</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Joinville is a city where part of the project takes place, especially in collaboration with UDESC and Univille for academic partnerships.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dac9ac0e037b36bcaa7b84fc97e0480a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779674647</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Laboratório Comunitário de Impressão 3D">
  <data key="d0">Laboratório Comunitário de Impressão 3D</data>
  <data key="d1">project</data>
  <data key="d2">The Laboratório Comunitário de Impressão 3D is a community project aimed at providing practical education and innovation opportunities related to 3D printing.&lt;SEP&gt;The Laboratório Comunitário de Impressão 3D is a community lab maintained by Karaguá Ecotech in Balneário Barra do Sul, aimed at fostering technological development.&lt;SEP&gt;The 3D Printing Community Laboratory is a project by Karaguá Ecotech aimed at accessible technological education for the community in Balneário Barra do Sul.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dac9ac0e037b36bcaa7b84fc97e0480a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96cfbacbd794cb84c14c05802c670b7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-644f99a306340252731a22af065c2b0e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779674750</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fundo Clima">
  <data key="d0">Fundo Clima</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fundo Clima is a fund aimed at supporting projects related to climate change mitigation and associated with the BNDES.&lt;SEP&gt;Fundo Clima is a climate fund that provides financing for carbon credit operations with specific conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Fundo Clima is an instrument of Brazil's National Policy on Climate Change (PNMC) that finances projects aimed at reducing greenhouse gas emissions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dac9ac0e037b36bcaa7b84fc97e0480a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35b161aec878c689605e9dc4ad34beb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68b29568543512fd2fc8ae0cbd127253</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779674838</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Salic">
  <data key="d0">Salic</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Salic is the official system used by the Ministry of Culture for project submission, management, and monitoring related to cultural sponsorship.&lt;SEP&gt;Salic is the official submission system for projects seeking financing through Lei Rouanet.&lt;SEP&gt;Salic is a system for the submission and management of projects that seek funding under the Ley Rouanet in Brazil.&lt;SEP&gt;Salic is the official system for submitting, monitoring, and managing cultural projects under the Lei Rouanet.&lt;SEP&gt;Salic refers to a system or guideline for detailing projects and processes, as mentioned in the text.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dac9ac0e037b36bcaa7b84fc97e0480a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35b161aec878c689605e9dc4ad34beb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-644f99a306340252731a22af065c2b0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68b29568543512fd2fc8ae0cbd127253&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4dc182d05fe8a824f6001879e64f17a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786227136</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gabriela">
  <data key="d0">Gabriela</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Gabriela is one of the engineers responsible for studies and technical analyses in the Karaguá Ecotech project.&lt;SEP&gt;Gabriela is an engineer involved in environmental characterization studies and supervision of monitoring technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Gabriela is an engineer responsible for environmental characterization studies of mangrove areas and oversees monitoring technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Gabriela is a member of the technical team involved in the project, participating directly in the processes of community engagement and development.&lt;SEP&gt;Gabriela is an engineer part of the technical team who is involved in discussions around ecobarrier design requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Gabriela is one of the engineers responsible for providing technical validation during the workshops.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dac9ac0e037b36bcaa7b84fc97e0480a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a80e4c81535ba4a7810a341f7875bc35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89141165cd3f083fc23989c3f15765c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47f28922da8d397aaccd4d34f84e64f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93daf61580b578c58a15dff9e12f4585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57e814d734f12e6e0e03507f0db90b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786227134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carol">
  <data key="d0">Carol</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Carol is an engineer involved in the research and development efforts related to the project at Karaguá Ecotech.&lt;SEP&gt;Carol is an engineer responsible for technical analyses that support the certification of carbon credits.&lt;SEP&gt;Carol is an engineer who conducts technical analyses to support the certification of carbon credits in collaboration with Verra.&lt;SEP&gt;Carol is part of the technical team, collaborating on research and implementation concerning the ecobarreira project.&lt;SEP&gt;Carol is an engineer part of the technical team who contributes to discussions on design parameters for the ecobarrier.&lt;SEP&gt;Carol is an engineer involved in the technical validation process alongside Gabriela and Sabrina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dac9ac0e037b36bcaa7b84fc97e0480a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a80e4c81535ba4a7810a341f7875bc35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89141165cd3f083fc23989c3f15765c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47f28922da8d397aaccd4d34f84e64f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93daf61580b578c58a15dff9e12f4585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57e814d734f12e6e0e03507f0db90b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786227134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sabrina">
  <data key="d0">Sabrina</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Sabrina is an engineer who plays a significant role in conducting studies and analyses for the Karaguá Ecotech initiative.&lt;SEP&gt;Sabrina is an engineer conducting scientific and operational field surveys.&lt;SEP&gt;Sabrina is an engineer leading scientific and operational field surveys, including assessments of priority areas for restoration.&lt;SEP&gt;Sabrina is a member of the technical team contributing to the development and testing of the ecobarreira alongside Gabriela and Carol.&lt;SEP&gt;Sabrina is another engineer from the team involved in the technical validation of ecobarrier design.&lt;SEP&gt;Sabrina is an engineer participating in the project, focusing on validation of the prototype's features.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dac9ac0e037b36bcaa7b84fc97e0480a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a80e4c81535ba4a7810a341f7875bc35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89141165cd3f083fc23989c3f15765c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47f28922da8d397aaccd4d34f84e64f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93daf61580b578c58a15dff9e12f4585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57e814d734f12e6e0e03507f0db90b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786227135</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Credenciais de Carbono Azul">
  <data key="d0">Credenciais de Carbono Azul</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Credenciais de Carbono Azul refers to the blue carbon credits generated through the conservation and restoration of mangrove ecosystems for sustainability initiatives.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dac9ac0e037b36bcaa7b84fc97e0480a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779674647</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Santa Catarina">
  <data key="d0">Santa Catarina</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Santa Catarina is a state in Brazil where Karaguá Ecotech operates its projects related to Carbon Blue and mangrove restoration.&lt;SEP&gt;Santa Catarina is a Brazilian state that has legislation (Lei nº 15.133/2010) recognizing Payment for Environmental Services (PSA) as a tool for sustainable development.&lt;SEP&gt;Santa Catarina is a state in Brazil where Karaguá Ecotech operates, particularly in carbon credit projects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96cfbacbd794cb84c14c05802c670b7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41caa912aa9f8b079fabe8c7285d8d78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10f1847a2487ac7c876527fa73acc8f6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779674963</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mangroves">
  <data key="d0">Mangroves</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Mangroves are coastal environments vital for carbon sequestration and provide numerous ecological benefits; they are the focus of Karaguá's projects.&lt;SEP&gt;Mangroves are coastal ecosystems that the project focuses on for restoration and monitoring activities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96cfbacbd794cb84c14c05802c670b7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89141165cd3f083fc23989c3f15765c4</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779674915</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BNDES Fundo Clima">
  <data key="d0">BNDES Fundo Clima</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">BNDES Fundo Clima is a financial fund that supports the operation of carbon credits within the context of Karaguá’s initiatives.&lt;SEP&gt;BNDES Fundo Clima is a Brazilian climate fund offering financial support for sustainable projects, including those related to blue carbon.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96cfbacbd794cb84c14c05802c670b7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8391c4fcd2580effc0f006b72bb8036</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779674687</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lei nº 15.133/2010">
  <data key="d0">Lei nº 15.133/2010</data>
  <data key="d1">legalregulation</data>
  <data key="d2">Lei nº 15.133/2010 is a state law that underpins the Payment for Environmental Services mechanisms employed by Karaguá to compensate local communities.&lt;SEP&gt;Lei nº 15.133/2010 is a state law in Santa Catarina that establishes the Política Estadual de Serviços Ambientais and the Programa Estadual de Pagamento por Serviços Ambientais (PEPSA).&lt;SEP&gt;Lei nº 15.133/2010 provides the legal framework for the Environmental Services Policy in SC and co-responsibility between public and private agents.&lt;SEP&gt;Lei nº 15.133/2010 establishes the State Policy on Environmental Services in Santa Catarina and recognizes PSA as a tool for sustainable development.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96cfbacbd794cb84c14c05802c670b7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41caa912aa9f8b079fabe8c7285d8d78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-801a0e33323bfe79b6cbfaaca8800a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89141165cd3f083fc23989c3f15765c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cf377716ee26ede13962ee6334fc04</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779674994</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Global Carbon Market">
  <data key="d0">Global Carbon Market</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Global Carbon Market refers to the international trading system for carbon credits, which experienced significant transactions and pricing trends in 2025.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8391c4fcd2580effc0f006b72bb8036</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779674687</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Credits de Carbono Azul">
  <data key="d0">Credits de Carbono Azul</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Credits de Carbono Azul are carbon credits generated from coastal ecosystems, recognized for their high storage capacity and socio-environmental co-benefits.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8391c4fcd2580effc0f006b72bb8036</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779674687</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lei nº 15.042/2024">
  <data key="d0">Lei nº 15.042/2024</data>
  <data key="d1">legalregulation</data>
  <data key="d2">Lei nº 15.042/2024 is Brazilian legislation that establishes a legal framework for a regulated carbon market in Brazil.&lt;SEP&gt;Lei nº 15.042/2024 is a law that established the regulatory framework for the Brazilian carbon market.&lt;SEP&gt;Lei nº 15.042/2024 is a Brazilian law that establishes the Sistema Brasileiro de Comércio de Emissões de Gases de Efeito Estufa, regulating the carbon market.&lt;SEP&gt;Lei nº 15.042/2024 creates a regulated carbon market in Brazil, impacting how carbon credits are managed and traded.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8391c4fcd2580effc0f006b72bb8036&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41caa912aa9f8b079fabe8c7285d8d78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-801a0e33323bfe79b6cbfaaca8800a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cf377716ee26ede13962ee6334fc04</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779674994</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="1,04 Bilhão de Dólares">
  <data key="d0">1,04 Bilhão de Dólares</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">1,04 Bilhão de Dólares refers to the estimated transaction volume of the voluntary carbon market in 2025.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8391c4fcd2580effc0f006b72bb8036</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779674687</data>
