</node>
<node id="R$ 42,5 Bilhões">
  <data key="d0">R$ 42,5 Bilhões</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">R$ 42,5 Bilhões represents the authorized funding amount from the BNDES for projects in 2026, available at a cost of 1% per year.&lt;SEP&gt;R$ 42,5 bilhões is the amount authorized by the Annual Budget Law for 2026, of which R$ 27 bilhões are allocated for loans.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8391c4fcd2580effc0f006b72bb8036&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68b29568543512fd2fc8ae0cbd127253</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779674838</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mercado Voluntário de Carbono">
  <data key="d0">Mercado Voluntário de Carbono</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Mercado Voluntário de Carbono is a voluntary carbon market where companies buy carbon credits on their initiative to offset emissions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8391c4fcd2580effc0f006b72bb8036</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779674688</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Brazilian Government">
  <data key="d0">Brazilian Government</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8391c4fcd2580effc0f006b72bb8036</data>
  <data key="d2">The Brazilian government established ProManguezal as a national program for conserving and sustainably using mangrove ecosystems in June 2024.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779674691</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manguezais Brasileiros">
  <data key="d0">Manguezais Brasileiros</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Manguezais Brasileiros are coastal ecosystems that store significant amounts of carbon and support numerous families, but lack economic returns for local residents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-41caa912aa9f8b079fabe8c7285d8d78</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779674709</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VM0033">
  <data key="d0">VM0033</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">VM0033 is an internationally recognized methodology for certifying carbon credits in coastal environments, specifically aimed at blue carbon initiatives.&lt;SEP&gt;VM0033 is a methodology for blue carbon certification used by Karaguá Ecotech.&lt;SEP&gt;VM0033 is a methodology for blue carbon accounting, applicable to the restoration of coastal wetlands.&lt;SEP&gt;VM0033 is a methodology recognized by Verra that supports the projects implemented by Karaguá Ecotech.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-41caa912aa9f8b079fabe8c7285d8d78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35b161aec878c689605e9dc4ad34beb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a80e4c81535ba4a7810a341f7875bc35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10f1847a2487ac7c876527fa73acc8f6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779674963</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VM0007/REDD+">
  <data key="d0">VM0007/REDD+</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">VM0007/REDD+ is another internationally recognized methodology utilized for certifying carbon credits, supporting sustainable forestry and conservation efforts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-41caa912aa9f8b079fabe8c7285d8d78</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779674709</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CRÉDITOS DE CARBONO">
  <data key="d0">CRÉDITOS DE CARBONO</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-41caa912aa9f8b079fabe8c7285d8d78</data>
  <data key="d2">The Baía da Babitonga represents a market potential for selling carbon credits derived from its extensive mangrove ecosystem.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779674715</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Créditos de Carbono Azul">
  <data key="d0">Créditos de Carbono Azul</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Blue carbon credits represent one ton of CO₂ equivalent that has been reduced, removed, or sequestered, and are a primary product of Karaguá Ecotech.&lt;SEP&gt;Créditos de Carbono Azul represents funding for carbon credit projects associated with blue carbon ecosystems.&lt;SEP&gt;Créditos de Carbono Azul refers to initiatives aimed at certifying blue carbon ecosystems, which are being monitored in the local territory for environmental purposes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35b161aec878c689605e9dc4ad34beb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68b29568543512fd2fc8ae0cbd127253&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de97259662535ffc45aa87131b91edcc</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786227134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VM0007">
  <data key="d0">VM0007</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">VM0007 is a REDD+ methodology used by Karaguá Ecotech for carbon credit certification.&lt;SEP&gt;VM0007 is the REDD+ methodology framework by Verra, initially focused on reducing emissions from deforestation and forest degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;VM0007 is a Verra methodology relevant to the carbon credit projects conducted by Karaguá Ecotech.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35b161aec878c689605e9dc4ad34beb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a80e4c81535ba4a7810a341f7875bc35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10f1847a2487ac7c876527fa73acc8f6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779674964</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BNDES">
  <data key="d0">BNDES</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">BNDES is a Brazilian development bank through which Karaguá Ecotech seeks funding via the Fundo Clima.&lt;SEP&gt;BNDES is the Brazilian Development Bank that manages the Fundo Clima and provides financing for climate-related projects.&lt;SEP&gt;BNDES is the Brazilian Development Bank, which is expected to provide funding for Karaguá Ecotech's expansion via the Climate Fund.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35b161aec878c689605e9dc4ad34beb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68b29568543512fd2fc8ae0cbd127253&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aabdb3200838b9e69e29cf6cafc7b6da</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779674942</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lei Estadual nº 15.133/2010">
  <data key="d0">Lei Estadual nº 15.133/2010</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">This state law regulates payment for environmental services and supports the community's involvement in environmental monitoring and restoration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35b161aec878c689605e9dc4ad34beb4</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779674732</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lei Rouanet">
  <data key="d0">Lei Rouanet</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lei Rouanet is a Brazilian law that provides tax incentives for cultural projects and supports funding through Salic.&lt;SEP&gt;Lei Rouanet is the primary tax incentive mechanism for culture in Brazil, enabling projects to attract resources from companies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35b161aec878c689605e9dc4ad34beb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68b29568543512fd2fc8ae0cbd127253</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779674838</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Municipalities">
  <data key="d0">Municipalities</data>
  <data key="d1">group</data>
  <data key="d2">Municipalities participate as partners in Karaguá Ecotech's model, receiving a share of the revenue generated from carbon credit sales.&lt;SEP&gt;Municipalities are local government entities mentioned as partners in the Karaguá Ecotech project.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35b161aec878c689605e9dc4ad34beb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026564c0148b51f6e4d359aee4d3338c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779674890</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Municípios">
  <data key="d0">Municípios</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Municípios refers to the municipalities that participate and share in the revenue of the carbon credit project, enhancing their role in governance and conservation efforts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35b161aec878c689605e9dc4ad34beb4</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779674732</data>
