<edge source="Karaguá Ecotech" target="Balneário Barra do Sul">
  <data key="d7">9.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation named Balneário Barra do Sul and Karaguá Ecotech refers to a collaborative initiative focused on environmental and educational projects in the coastal region of Balneário Barra do Sul, Brazil. At the heart of this collaboration is a pilot project undertaken by Karaguá Ecotech, which is specifically designed to validate a conservation model while generating carbon credits.

Karaguá Ecotech's pilot project encompasses 380 hectares of land and is centered around mangrove restoration, an essential environmental effort in the region. The project seeks to engage the local community actively, promoting participation through governance and restoration activities that enhance environmental awareness and community involvement.

The pilot project serves multiple purposes: it not only aims to demonstrate the effectiveness of Karaguá Ecotech's operational model on-site but also fosters educational initiatives aimed at the surrounding community. By integrating conservation efforts with local governance, Karaguá Ecotech seeks to build a sustainable framework that balances ecological restoration with community development. 

Overall, the partnership between Balneário Barra do Sul and Karaguá Ecotech represents a comprehensive strategy to achieve environmental goals while supporting local community engagement through innovative restoration practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Karaguá's pilot project is initiated in Balneário Barra do Sul, focusing on mangrove restoration.</data>
  <data key="d9">carbon credit,community involvement,educational initiative,expansion project,initial pilot,initiation site,local operation,model validation,operational area,operational scale,partnership,pilot project,project initiation,project location</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ab5216ced144c274bc01b9f76450bfe1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dac9ac0e037b36bcaa7b84fc97e0480a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41caa912aa9f8b079fabe8c7285d8d78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfd11d7c2c4bd3494e41a898407867fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daf3f3a511399d27baaafacc8a1db9af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89141165cd3f083fc23989c3f15765c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aabdb3200838b9e69e29cf6cafc7b6da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10f1847a2487ac7c876527fa73acc8f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cf377716ee26ede13962ee6334fc04</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1779674999</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Karaguá Ecotech" target="Baía da Babitonga">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Karaguá Ecotech is focusing on Baía da Babitonga for scalable Blue Carbon project opportunities due to its ecological importance.&lt;SEP&gt;Karaguá Ecotech aims to expand its projects in Baía da Babitonga due to its significant mangrove area.&lt;SEP&gt;Baía da Babitonga is identified as an area where Karaguá Ecotech could implement a significant mangrove conservation project.&lt;SEP&gt;Karaguá Ecotech aims to expand its operations to Baía da Babitonga, leveraging the ecological significance of the area.&lt;SEP&gt;Karaguá Ecotech aims to expand its environmental restoration efforts to a target area of up to 8,000 hectares in Baía da Babitonga.&lt;SEP&gt;Baía da Babitonga is targeted for expansion by Karaguá Ecotech for significant mangrove restoration efforts.</data>
  <data key="d9">conservation project,ecological focus,ecological importance,ecological significance,environmental restoration,estuary restoration,expansion focus,expansion goal,project expansion</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ab5216ced144c274bc01b9f76450bfe1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96cfbacbd794cb84c14c05802c670b7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41caa912aa9f8b079fabe8c7285d8d78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfd11d7c2c4bd3494e41a898407867fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aabdb3200838b9e69e29cf6cafc7b6da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cf377716ee26ede13962ee6334fc04</data>
